From cb7c762284b08b3c305a8c8cb9fea5078017598e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:19:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A page opened at a #place goes there in one step, not a glide
 that overshoots

Opening index.html#menu, #farm (and first-visit.html#parking and the like) started a
SMOOTH glide, because html{scroll-behavior:smooth} also smooths the browser's first
jump to the #place, made while the page is still being built. The glide ran past the
place by 130 to 2,400 px (more on some runs) and stayed there until keepHashTarget put
the place back 1.5 s after the load.

css/styles.css: html:not(.wa-ready){scroll-behavior:auto}. js/features.js
(keepHashTarget, which runs on all six pages): puts wa-ready on <html> after the load
(no #place, reload, Back) or, on a page opened at a #place, after its two re-scrolls
(0.3 s and 1.5 s after the load, which stay as the backstop). Links on the page glide
as before once the class is there. Without JavaScript the page jumps instead of gliding.

tests/hash-open.test.mjs (new, order 394, row in tests/README.md): looks at every frame
until 2 s after the load, laptop and phone, English and Spanish, a sandboxed preview
frame, reduced motion, home page and First visit. 11 of its 29 checks fail without the
fix and all pass with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
