 | `nav-highlight` | the top menu (about two minutes): Seasons, Tomatoes, Pizza, GreenHouse and Shop each land on their own section and light up only their own link, going down the page and back up, with smooth scrolling on. On the page itself and inside a sandboxed frame from another address, the way the claude.ai preview shows the site (there, going back up used to light the link above: Pizza lit Tomatoes). Also a short (500px) and a tall (1400px) window, Spanish, Vietnamese, Hindi and Chinese (a click anywhere on a link reaches that link, not a neighbour's 44px tap area), and the menu behind the menu button on a phone and in a narrow or zoomed-in window |
 | `anchor-landing` | where a link to a place on the same page puts that place (about five minutes): on the usual line under the sticky header, 88 px on a computer and 80 px on a phone, the same for every link, with smooth scrolling on and a page that has just opened (so the boxes below were never on the screen). The menu's On the Farm and the places after it, the Pizza reservations button, the Fall & holidays and Farm visit buttons of the Shop, on a laptop, a full HD screen, a narrow window and a phone, in English and Spanish, inside a sandboxed frame from another address (the claude.ai preview) and with reduced motion; a page opened at a place (`index.html#menu`, a QR code); the Drive time box and the signup block, which sit inside a fading box. The First visit page: the four cards of Good to know (Parking, Bathrooms, Dogs, Strollers & wheelchairs) on the same line, from the quick links and from a page opened at `first-visit.html#parking`. Fails when a box that fades in leaves its link 26 px too high (the hidden box is drawn 26 px lower when the browser works out where to scroll: `.reveal` in `css/styles.css`) or when a place has a scroll margin of its own on top of the page's `scroll-padding-top` (the cards of First visit had one and landed 88 px too low) |
+| `hash-open` | a page opened at an address with a #place (about one minute): a link from another page, the questions that link into First visit, a QR code, a shared link. Every frame is looked at in real time from the start until 2 s after the load, with smooth scrolling left on. The page must go to the place in one step and stay (never more than 40 px from where it ends), and the place must end on the usual line (88 px on a computer, 80 px on a phone). On a laptop and a phone, in English and Spanish, in a sandboxed frame from another address (the claude.ai preview), with reduced motion, on the home page (`#menu`, `#farm`, `#varieties`) and on First visit (`#parking`, `#checklist`, `#strollers`). Also that links on the page glide again once the page has loaded. Fails when the browser's first jump is smoothed (`html{scroll-behavior:smooth}` while the page is still being built): the page glided past the place by 130 to 2,400 px and stayed there until the page put the place back 1.5 s after the load. The fix holds smooth scrolling back until `<html>` has `wa-ready` (`css/styles.css`, `keepHashTarget` in `js/features.js`) |
 | `colour-blind` | colour-blind visitors (about 75 s): the home page photographed as Chrome shows it for protanopia, deuteranopia, tritanopia and no colour at all; the current language in the language menu, the chosen season above the hero, the chosen season in the "What's on the farm" table, the open days of the week strip and the chosen place in the map list must each differ from the others by a shape (a dark ring, edge or line: contrast 3 or more in every view), not by colour alone; every link inside running text is underlined. A deliberate mistake (the ring taken away) is caught first. The full table is in `docs/COLOUR_BLIND_CHECK.md` |
